SOL grid points in n_r   [-]\nflag for PRL model calculation \n=0: no drift \n=1: Parks 2000 drift \n=2: Baylor 2007 drift \n=3: HPI2 drift \nNumber of PRL cloudlets from pellet [-]\nID number of PRL cloudlet for diag output [-]\nflag for drift scalings\ninjection angle for HPI2 drift\n.. for HPI2 drift\nplasma elongation integer, intent(in), optional :: KAPPA number of fast ion species (H,D,T,He3,He4) [-]\nnumber of energy groups for fast ions [-]\ncharge of fast ions (1,2) [-]\nNumber of SOL grid points in n_r   [-]\nflag for PRL model calculation \n=0: no drift \n=1: Parks 2000 drift \n=2: Baylor 2007 drift \n=3: HPI2 drift \nNumber of PRL cloudlets from pellet [-]\nID number of PRL cloudlet for diag output [-]\nflag for drift scalings\ninjection angle for HPI2 drift\n.. for HPI2 drift\nplasma elongation real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: DEL_DRIFT time of pellet entry to path cells [s]\npellet effective radius at exit from path cells [m]\nsource rate in path cells [/s]\nelectron density at entrance to path cells [keV]\nelectron density at exit from path cells [keV]\nelectron temperature at entrance to path cells [keV]\nelectron temperature at exit from path cells [keV]\nresulting density deposition from PRL [/m**3]\ndrift calculated from HPI2 scaling Declartation of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/pellet.html"},{"title":"AJAX_LOAD_RZBDY – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_LOAD_RZBDY(r0, a0, s0, e0, e1, d1, iflag, message, NRHO_AJAX, NTHETA_AJAX, NKLAM_AJAX, RHOMAX_AJAX) AJAX_LOAD_RZBDY converts geometric boundary and axial constraints to values of\n  the R,Z coordinates then calls AJAX_LOAD_RZLAM to fill in the profiles References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Declaration of input variables\nCheck optional input\nAllocate and set poloidal mode information Convert from geometric to moments quantities Moments triangularity ~geometric triangularity/4\nIterate for triangularity value, convergence is fast and robust\nOver iteration Over iteration Elongation Fill in radial values of R,Z expansion coefficients Allocate radial grid and R,Z arrays\nSet radial grid\nRadial variation\nOver radial nodes Over radial nodes Load private data\nCheck messages Cleanup and exit Deallocate mode information\nDeallocate grid and R,Z arrays Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r0 major radius of geometric center [m]\nminor radius in midplane [m]\naxis shift normalized to a0 [-]\naxis elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge triangularity normalized to a0 [-] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: a0 major radius of geometric center [m]\nminor radius in midplane [m]\naxis shift normalized to a0 [-]\naxis elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge triangularity normalized to a0 [-] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: s0 major radius of geometric center [m]\nminor radius in midplane [m]\naxis shift normalized to a0 [-]\naxis elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge triangularity normalized to a0 [-] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: e0 major radius of geometric center [m]\nminor radius in midplane [m]\naxis shift normalized to a0 [-]\naxis elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge triangularity normalized to a0 [-] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: e1 major radius of geometric center [m]\nminor radius in midplane [m]\naxis shift normalized to a0 [-]\naxis elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge triangularity normalized to a0 [-] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: d1 major radius of geometric center [m]\nminor radius in midplane [m]\naxis shift normalized to a0 [-]\naxis elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge elongation normalized to a0 [-]\nedge triangularity normalized to a0 [-] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional input variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] integer, intent(in), optional :: NRHO_AJAX no. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of lambda modes in nternal data [-]\n=5 default integer, intent(in), optional :: NTHETA_AJAX no. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of lambda modes in nternal data [-]\n=5 default integer, intent(in), optional :: NKLAM_AJAX no. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of lambda modes in nternal data [-]\n=5 default real(kind=rspec), intent(in), optional :: RHOMAX_AJAX value of internal radial grid at R,Z boundary [rho]\n=1.0 default Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_load_rzbdy.html"},{"title":"AJAX_LOAD_RZLAM – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_LOAD_RZLAM(nr_rz, nk_rz, rho_rz, m, n, r, z, iflag, message, K_GRID, L_MFILTER_AJAX, NRHO_AJAX, NTHETA_AJAX, NZETA_AJAX, RHOMAX_AJAX, NR_LAM, NK_LAM, RHO_LAM, LAM) AJAX_LOAD_RZLAM loads 2D/3D MHD equilibria in inverse coordinate form References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004\n  W.A.Houlberg, named DO loop on EXIT 1/2005 Comments:\n  Knowledge of the form of the input radial grid (see K_GRID) is necessary for\n    accurate mapping to the internal grid\n  The internal radial grid, rho_3d, is proportional to the square root of the\n    toroidal flux\n  The maximum value of the R,Z radial grid defines rho/rhomax=1\n  The internal radial grid will be scaled to rhomax if specified, otherwise it\n    will default to the domain [0,1]\n  The input poloidal and toroidal mode numbers are the same for the R,Z and\n    lambda expansions and dimensioned to the greater of the two; e.g., if there\n    are more poloidal and toroidal modes for the input lambda they should be\n    appended to the end of the sequence of values for the R,Z expansions\n  Mode filtering may be tried to improve calculations near the axis and the\n    outer boundary Declaration of input variables\nSet number of angular modes\nSet the number of toroidal field periods, < 100 periods\nOver modes Find lowest non-zero toroidal mode number\nOver modes Found no peiodicity in data, set to axisymmetric\nNon-axisymmetric \nCheck periodicity\nOver modes Some mode does not fit the periodicity\nOver modes Check optional input for internal grid initialization Set the number of internal radial nodes\nUse input value\nUse default value\nSet the number of internal poloidal nodes\nUse input value\nMake sure the number of modes is odd for 4th order Simpson integration\nAxisymmetric\n4k+1 typically yields <0.1% error in B_zeta = RB_t ~ const\nNon-axisymmetric\nError estimate yet to be quantified, typically |m| <= 8\nSet the number of internal toroidal nodes\nUse input value\nMake sure the number of modes is odd for 4th order Simpson integration\nUse axisymmetric value\nUse non-axisymmetric default value\nError estimate yet to be quantified, typically |n/nper| <= 5\nSet the option for mode filtering\nUse input value\nUse default value Set general information and initialize arrays Scale the outer radial boundary of R,Z to rhomax\nUse input value\nUse default value\nSet the mode numbers of the (m,n)=(0,0) and (m,n)=(1,0) modes\nOver modes Call initialization routine Poloidal and toroidal mode data Initialization\nCopy data\nSet |m| with mode filtering for rho**|m| normalization\nOver modes Check for filtering\nFiltering for |m| > 3\nEven mode, remove rho 2\nOdd mode, remove rho 3\nOver modes Load R and Z expansion data Initialization\nMake copy of radial grid and expansion coefficients\nIf the user does not provide an axial value for R,Z data, need to fill in\nAllocate radial grid and R,Z arrays, add radial node at axis\nAllocate radial grid and R,Z arrays, use input grid\nConvert rho to sqrt(toroidal flux) if necesssary and scale\n~toroidal flux\n~sqrt(toroidal flux)\nUnallowed choice of input grid\nSet the inner radial boundary of R,Z for checking axial extrapolation\nAllocate spline arrays\nNormalize the expansion coefficients to rho**m\nOver modes Over radial nodes Over radial nodes Parabolic extrapolation to axis (user values ignored)\nMap R_mn to internal radial grid\nCheck messages\nRespline the R coeffs for internal storage\nMap Z_mn to internal radial grid\nCheck messages\nRespline the Z coeffs for internal storage\nOver modes Set the length scale factors Magnetic stream function Load lambda from input\nCheck messages\nCalculate lambdas for axisymmetric plasma\nSet up 3d grid for flux surface integrals\nCheck messages\nCalculate lambda\nNeed to specify stream function for non-axisymmetric plasmas Cleanup and exit Deallocate radial grid and R,Z arrays\nDeallocate spline arrays Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nr_rz no. of radial nodes in the input R,Z [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input R,Z [-]\npoloidal mode numbers [-]\ntoroidal mode numbers [-] integer, intent(in) :: nk_rz no. of radial nodes in the input R,Z [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input R,Z [-]\npoloidal mode numbers [-]\ntoroidal mode numbers [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rho_rz (:) radial nodes in the input R,Z [arb]\nexpansion coeffs for R [m]\nexpansion coeffs for Z [m] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(in) :: m (:) no. of radial nodes in the input R,Z [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input R,Z [-]\npoloidal mode numbers [-]\ntoroidal mode numbers [-] integer, intent(in) :: n (:) no. of radial nodes in the input R,Z [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input R,Z [-]\npoloidal mode numbers [-]\ntoroidal mode numbers [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r (:,:) radial nodes in the input R,Z [arb]\nexpansion coeffs for R [m]\nexpansion coeffs for Z [m] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: z (:,:) radial nodes in the input R,Z [arb]\nexpansion coeffs for R [m]\nexpansion coeffs for Z [m] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional input variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] integer, intent(in), optional :: K_GRID option designating type of input radial grid [-]\n=0 proportional to sqrt(toroidal flux)\n=1 proportional to toroidal flux\n=else not allowed\nno. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of toroidal nodes per period in internal data [odd]\n=11 default for non-axisymmetric plasma\n=0 default for axisymmetric plasma\nno. of radial nodes in the input lambda [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input lambda [-] logical, intent(in), optional :: L_MFILTER_AJAX option for mode filtering [logical] integer, intent(in), optional :: NRHO_AJAX option designating type of input radial grid [-]\n=0 proportional to sqrt(toroidal flux)\n=1 proportional to toroidal flux\n=else not allowed\nno. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of toroidal nodes per period in internal data [odd]\n=11 default for non-axisymmetric plasma\n=0 default for axisymmetric plasma\nno. of radial nodes in the input lambda [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input lambda [-] integer, intent(in), optional :: NTHETA_AJAX option designating type of input radial grid [-]\n=0 proportional to sqrt(toroidal flux)\n=1 proportional to toroidal flux\n=else not allowed\nno. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of toroidal nodes per period in internal data [odd]\n=11 default for non-axisymmetric plasma\n=0 default for axisymmetric plasma\nno. of radial nodes in the input lambda [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input lambda [-] integer, intent(in), optional :: NZETA_AJAX option designating type of input radial grid [-]\n=0 proportional to sqrt(toroidal flux)\n=1 proportional to toroidal flux\n=else not allowed\nno. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of toroidal nodes per period in internal data [odd]\n=11 default for non-axisymmetric plasma\n=0 default for axisymmetric plasma\nno. of radial nodes in the input lambda [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input lambda [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in), optional :: RHOMAX_AJAX value of internal radial grid at R,Z boundary [rho]\n=1.0 default\nradial nodes in the input lambda [arb]\nexpansion coeffs for lambda [-] Declaration of local variables integer, intent(in), optional :: NR_LAM option designating type of input radial grid [-]\n=0 proportional to sqrt(toroidal flux)\n=1 proportional to toroidal flux\n=else not allowed\nno. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of toroidal nodes per period in internal data [odd]\n=11 default for non-axisymmetric plasma\n=0 default for axisymmetric plasma\nno. of radial nodes in the input lambda [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input lambda [-] integer, intent(in), optional :: NK_LAM option designating type of input radial grid [-]\n=0 proportional to sqrt(toroidal flux)\n=1 proportional to toroidal flux\n=else not allowed\nno. of radial nodes in internal data [-]\n=21 default\nno. of poloidal nodes in internal data [odd]\n=21 default\nno. of toroidal nodes per period in internal data [odd]\n=11 default for non-axisymmetric plasma\n=0 default for axisymmetric plasma\nno. of radial nodes in the input lambda [-]\nno. of poloidal & toroidal modes in the input lambda [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in), optional :: RHO_LAM (:) value of internal radial grid at R,Z boundary [rho]\n=1.0 default\nradial nodes in the input lambda [arb]\nexpansion coeffs for lambda [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in), optional :: LAM (:,:) value of internal radial grid at R,Z boundary [rho]\n=1.0 default\nradial nodes in the input lambda [arb]\nexpansion coeffs for lambda [-] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_load_rzlam.html"},{"title":"AJAX_LOAD_MAGFLUX – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_LOAD_MAGFLUX(phitot, k_pflx, nr_pflx, rho_pflx, pflx, iflag, message) AJAX_LOAD_MAGFLUX loads magnetic flux data References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Declaration of input variables Iotabar allocation Radial dimension\nIf storage requirements have changed, reallocate\nReallocate iotabar\nAllocate iotabar Total toroidal flux in private data Set iotabar in private data Initialize\niotabar input\nd(Psi)/d(rho) input\nq input\nInterpolate iotabar onto internal grid\nCheck messages\nGet spline coefficients on internal grid\nIf value at origin not supplied, overwrite with approximation Set signs of poloidal and toroidal magnetic fields Set logical switches for flux surface averaging Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: phitot radial nodes in input flux [rho]\npoloidal magnetic flux function\n=q [-]\n=iotabar [-]\n=d(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(in) :: k_pflx option for represention of poloidal flux [-]\n=1 iotabar (rotational transform)\n=2 d(Psi)/d(rho)\n=else q (safety factor)\nno. of radial nodes in input flux [-] integer, intent(in) :: nr_pflx option for represention of poloidal flux [-]\n=1 iotabar (rotational transform)\n=2 d(Psi)/d(rho)\n=else q (safety factor)\nno. of radial nodes in input flux [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rho_pflx (:) radial nodes in input flux [rho]\npoloidal magnetic flux function\n=q [-]\n=iotabar [-]\n=d(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: pflx (:) radial nodes in input flux [rho]\npoloidal magnetic flux function\n=q [-]\n=iotabar [-]\n=d(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of local variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character]","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_load_magflux.html"},{"title":"AJAX_CAR2CYL – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_CAR2CYL(r_car, r_cyl) AJAX_CAR2CYL converts from Cartesian to cylindrical coordinates References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Declaration of input variables Cartesian to cylindrical conversion R\nphi\nZ Ensure 0 <= phi <= 2*pi Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r_car (:) Cartesian coordinates (x,y,z) [m,m,m] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out) :: r_cyl (:) cylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m] Initialization Null output","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_car2cyl.html"},{"title":"AJAX_CYL2CAR – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_CYL2CAR(r_cyl, r_car) AJAX_CYL2CAR converts from cylindrical to Cartesian coordinates References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Declaration of input variables Cylindrical to Cartesian conversion x\ny\nz Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r_cyl (:) cylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out) :: r_car (:) Cartesian coordinates (x,y,z) [m,m,m] Initialization Null output","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_cyl2car.html"},{"title":"AJAX_CYL2FLX – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_CYL2FLX(r_cyl, r_flx, iflag, message, G_CYL, GSQRT, TAU) AJAX_CYL2FLX converts from cylindrical to flux coordinates References:\n  S.E.Attenberger, W.A.Houlberg, S.P.Hirshman J Comp Phys 72 (1987) 435\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Comments:\n  The basic method is a Newton iteration in 2 dimensions\n  Input values of r_flx are used as an initial guess\n  Convergence is typically one order of magnitude reduction in the\n    error in R and Z per iteration - should rarely exceed 5 iterations\n  The toroidal angle in flux coordinates is the same as in cylindrical\n    coordinates giving a right-handed system with positive Jacobian\n  Point 0 is the previous best guess and point 1 is a trial point\n  If point 1 is further from (R,Z) than point 0, a new trial point is\n    generated by halving the step and using interpolated derivatives Declaration of input variables\nCoordinates and metrics for iteration\nTolerance for convergence\nMaximum iterations\nGrid halving index\nSet flux coordinate toroidal angle equal to cylindrical angle\nSet starting points and parameters\nMove rho away from axis if necessary Iterate to find flux coordinates Over iteration Get cylindrical coordinates at point 1\nCheck messages\nCheck convergence\nConverged, but first check if solution is in the R,Z domain\nSolution is at point 1, copy to output arrays and exit\nNeed improved estimate for rho and theta and get new Jacobian\nNo solution exists for the Newton method\nAssume the solution is at the origin where tau=0\nCheck consistency of sign of Jacobian\nBad data\nCheck whether convergence is improving\nConverging, double step if possible and set point 0 = point 1\nNot converging - halve step\nCalculate new rho and theta steps\nUse empirical combination of last two steps to avoid oscillation\n0 and 1 may coincide here\nProject to desired point using Jacobian information\ndrho=(R_theta dZ-Z_theta dR)/tau\ndtheta=(Z_rho dR-R_rho dZ)/tau\nSet flux coordinates for new point 1\nStepped past minor axis, flip flux coordinates\nOver iteration Exceeded maximum iterations Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r_cyl (:) cylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m] Declaration of input/output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(inout) :: r_flx (:) flux coordinates (rho,theta,zeta) [rho,rad,rad] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional output variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: G_CYL (:) R,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ]\n3D Jacobian [m 3/rho]\n2D Jacobian in phi=zeta=constant plane [m 2/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: GSQRT R,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ]\n3D Jacobian [m 3/rho]\n2D Jacobian in phi=zeta=constant plane [m 2/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: TAU R,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ]\n3D Jacobian [m 3/rho]\n2D Jacobian in phi=zeta=constant plane [m 2/rho] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_cyl2flx.html"},{"title":"AJAX_FLX2CYL – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_FLX2CYL(r_flx, r_cyl, iflag, message, G_CYL, GSQRT, TAU) AJAX_FLX2CYL converts from flux to cylindrical coordinates References:\n  S.E.Attenberger, W.A.Houlberg, S.P.Hirshman J Comp Phys 72 (1987) 435\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Comments:\n  The representation is extended beyond the rho_3d grid by linear\n    extrapolation of the m=1, n=0 term in rho, with all other terms\n    held fixed at the edge value\n  This permits unique representation of all space for flux surfaces\n    that are everywhere convex (does not include bean-shapes)\n  rho**m is factored out of the Fourier coefficients prior to spline\n    fitting for increased accuracy near the origin\n  Mode filtering is used to improve calculations near the axis and the outer\n    boundary Declaration of input variables\nNull local values\nphi = zeta\nLimit to R,Z domain\nAxial resolution Evaluate R,Z and derivatives Loop over modes\nOver modes Set sine and cosine values\nCalculate rho m and its derivative\nrho 0\nInside last closed surface, rho |m|\nOutside last closed surface, rhomax |m|\nR_mn and dR_mn/drho from spline fits\nZ_mn and dZ_mn/drho from spline fits\nR = sum_mn [ R_mn * cos(m theta-n zeta) * rho m ]\nZ = sum_mn [ Z_mn * sin(m theta-n zeta) * rho m ]\ndR/dtheta = sum_mn [ -m * R_mn * sin(m theta-n zeta) * rho m ]\ndR/dzeta = sum_mn [ n * R_mn * sin(m theta-n zeta) * rho m ]\ndZ/dtheta = sum_mn [ m * Z_mn * cos(m theta-n zeta) * rho m ]\ndZ/dtheta = sum_mn [ -n * Z_mn * cos(m theta-n zeta) * rho m ]\nRadial derivatives inside R,Z domain\ndR/drho = sum_mn [ rho m * dR_mn/drho + R_mn *d(rho m)/drho ]\n                   * cos(m theta-n zeta)\ndZ/drho = sum_mn [ rho m * dZ_mn/drho + Z_mn *d(rho m)/drho ]\n                   * sin(m theta-n zeta)\nOver modes Radial derivatives outside R,Z domain\nThis point is off the grid toward the wall Optional output R,Z derivatives\n2D Jacobian = dR/dtheta * dZ/drho - dR/drho * dZ/dtheta\n3D Jacobian = R * tau Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r_flx (:) flux coordinates (rho,theta,zeta) [rho,rad,rad] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out) :: r_cyl (:) cylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m] Declaration of optional output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: G_CYL (:) R,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ]\n3D Jacobian [m 3/rho]\n2D Jacobian in phi=zeta=constant plane [m 2/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: GSQRT R,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ]\n3D Jacobian [m 3/rho]\n2D Jacobian in phi=zeta=constant plane [m 2/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: TAU R,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ]\n3D Jacobian [m 3/rho]\n2D Jacobian in phi=zeta=constant plane [m 2/rho] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_flx2cyl.html"},{"title":"AJAX_B – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_B(r_flx, r_cyl, g_cyl, iflag, message, B_CON, B_CO, B_CYL, B_CAR, B_POL, B_TOR, B_MOD) AJAX_B gets components of B in various forms References:\n  S.E.Attenberger, W.A.Houlberg, S.P.Hirshman, J Comp Phys 72 (1987) 435\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Declaration of input variables Set primary variables 3D Jacobian = R * (dR/dtheta * dZ/drho - dR/drho * dZ/dtheta)\nMagnetic stream function derivatives\nRotational transform and derivative of toroidal flux\nCheck messages Contravariant components B&#94;rho\nB&#94;theta\nB&#94;zeta Cylindrical components B_R\nB_phi\nB_Z Covariant components B_rho\nB_theta\nB_zeta Cartesian components B_x\nB_y\nB_z Poloidal field B_pol Toroidal field B_tor |B| B_mod Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r_flx (:) flux coordinates (rho,theta,zeta) [rho,rad,rad]\ncylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m]\nR,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: r_cyl (:) flux coordinates (rho,theta,zeta) [rho,rad,rad]\ncylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m]\nR,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: g_cyl (:) flux coordinates (rho,theta,zeta) [rho,rad,rad]\ncylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m]\nR,Z derivatives\n=(R_rho,R_theta,R_zeta,Z_rho,Z_theta,Z_zeta)\n [m/rho,m,      m,     m/rho,m,      m     ] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional output variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: B_CON (:) contravariant (B&#94;rho,B&#94;theta,B&#94;zeta) [T rho/m,T/m,T/m]\ncovariant (B_rho,B_theta,B_zeta) [T m/rho,T m,T m]\ncylindrical (B_R,B_phi,B_Z) [T,T,T]\nCartesian (B_x,B_y,B_z) [T,T,T]\npoloidal field [T]\ntoroidal field [T]\n|B| [T] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: B_CO (:) contravariant (B&#94;rho,B&#94;theta,B&#94;zeta) [T rho/m,T/m,T/m]\ncovariant (B_rho,B_theta,B_zeta) [T m/rho,T m,T m]\ncylindrical (B_R,B_phi,B_Z) [T,T,T]\nCartesian (B_x,B_y,B_z) [T,T,T]\npoloidal field [T]\ntoroidal field [T]\n|B| [T] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: B_CYL (:) contravariant (B&#94;rho,B&#94;theta,B&#94;zeta) [T rho/m,T/m,T/m]\ncovariant (B_rho,B_theta,B_zeta) [T m/rho,T m,T m]\ncylindrical (B_R,B_phi,B_Z) [T,T,T]\nCartesian (B_x,B_y,B_z) [T,T,T]\npoloidal field [T]\ntoroidal field [T]\n|B| [T] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: B_CAR (:) contravariant (B&#94;rho,B&#94;theta,B&#94;zeta) [T rho/m,T/m,T/m]\ncovariant (B_rho,B_theta,B_zeta) [T m/rho,T m,T m]\ncylindrical (B_R,B_phi,B_Z) [T,T,T]\nCartesian (B_x,B_y,B_z) [T,T,T]\npoloidal field [T]\ntoroidal field [T]\n|B| [T] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: B_POL contravariant (B&#94;rho,B&#94;theta,B&#94;zeta) [T rho/m,T/m,T/m]\ncovariant (B_rho,B_theta,B_zeta) [T m/rho,T m,T m]\ncylindrical (B_R,