2_R, GRTH_R, SUS11_R, SUS12_R, SUS21_R, SUS22_R) AJAX_FLUXAV_B gets flux surface quantities that depend on B References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004\n  W.A.Houlberg, named DO loop on EXIT 1/2005 Declaration of input variables Check whether flux surface averaging arrays have been set Check messages Check whether values outside R,Z domain are requested (nr is last point inside) on internal grid for b2_r, ftrap_r, and fm_r Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid \nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis Theta and gam=n.grad(Theta) for Fm and n.grad(Theta) in axisymmetric plasmas Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid \nOver radial nodes Over poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis Initialization\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain <1/B**2> Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid \nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain Initialization\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain f_trap Initialization\n<|B|> and B_max\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nUpper and lower trapped fractions bound solution\nOver radial nodes Flux surface average for upper estimate of trapped fraction\nOver toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Trapped fraction normalized to sqrt(rho) = 0.25 f_trap_low + 0.75 f_trap_upper\nOver radial nodes Extrapolate to axis using constant normalized trapped fraction \nFind index of first point away from axis in R,Z domain\nOver radial nodes Over radial nodes Interpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence F_m Initialization\nNon-axisymmetric plasma\nq(rho) for fm_1 interpolation\nOver radial nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence\nIf first node is not at the axis, include in calculation\nOver radial nodes fm_r(2)=eps 1.5\nfm_r(1)=R_0*q/eps 1.5\nOver radial nodes Axisymmetric plasma\nOver poloidal moments Over radial nodes sin(Theta) terms\nOver poloidal nodes d(B)/d(theta) at end points noting periodicity\nsin(m Theta) B&#94;theta/B*(dB/dtheta)\nOver poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes sin(m Theta) B&#94;theta*(dB/dtheta)\nOver poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes cos(Theta) terms\nOver poloidal nodes d(B)/d(theta) at end points noting periodicity\ncos(m Theta) B&#94;theta/B*(dB/dtheta)\nOver poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes cos(m Theta) B&#94;theta*(dB/dtheta)\nOver poloidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Multiply by 2/ / and normalize to rho**1.5\nOver radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence\nOver poloidal moments n.grad(Theta) Initialization\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain Susceptance matrix element S11 Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Remove dominant radial dependence\nOver toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence Susceptance matrix element S12 Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Remove dominant radial dependence\nOver toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence Susceptance matrix element S21 Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Remove dominant radial dependence\nOver toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence Susceptance matrix element S22 Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Remove dominant radial dependence\nOver toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence\nIf first node is not at the axis, include in calculation Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nrho_r no. of radial nodes [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rho_r (:) radial nodes [rho] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional output variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: B2_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: BM2_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: FM_R (:,:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: FTRAP_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: GR2BM2_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: GRTH_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: SUS11_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: SUS12_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: SUS21_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: SUS22_R (:) [T 2]\n<1/B 2> [/T 2]\npoloidal moments of <[n.grad(B)] 2>/ [-]\ntrapped particle fraction [-] [rho 2/m 2/T**2]\nn.grad(Theta) [/m]\nsuceptance matrix element 11 (pol-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 12 (pol-tor) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 21 (tor-pol) [-]\nsuceptance matrix element 22 (tor-tor) [-] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_fluxav_b.html"},{"title":"AJAX_FLUXAV_G – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_FLUXAV_G(nrho_r, rho_r, iflag, message, AREA_R, DVOL_R, GRHO1_R, GRHO2_R, GRHO2RM2_R, RM2_R, VOL_R, VP_R) AJAX_FLUXAV_G gets flux surface quantities that depend on geometry References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004\n  W.A.Houlberg, named DO loop on EXIT 1/2005 Declaration of input variables\nCheck whether flux surface averaging arrays have been set\nCheck messages\nCheck whether values outside R,Z domain are requested (nr is last point inside)\nOver nodes Over nodes d(V)/d(rho) on user grid for area_r, dvol_r, vol_r and vp_r Initialization\nRemove dominant radial dependence\nExtrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain\nReintroduce dominant radial dependence <|grad(rho)|> on user grid for area_r and grho1_r Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Interpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain Area Initialization\nUse temporary arrays delta(Volume) Initialization\nCalculate from integral rho drho (V'/rho), where (V'/rho) is a weak function\nAllow for first node to be away from the axis\nFirst node is off axis\nFirst node is on axis\nOver radial nodes Over radial nodes Set ghost node value equal to last node <|grad(rho)|> Initialization\nCopy from temporary array Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain <1/R**2> Initialization\nCalculate on internal grid\nOver radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate to axis\nInterpolate to user grid inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to user grid outside R,Z domain Volume Initialization\nSum up dvol elements\nAllow for first node to be away from the axis\nFirst node is off axis\nFirst node is on axis\nOver radial nodes Over radial nodes d(Volume)/d(rho) Initialization\nCopy from temporary array Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nrho_r no. of radial nodes [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rho_r (:) radial nodes [rho] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional output variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: AREA_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: DVOL_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: GRHO1_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: GRHO2_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: GRHO2RM2_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: RM2_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: VOL_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: VP_R (:) surface area [m 2]\ncell volume between rho_r(i) and rho_r(i+1) [m 3]\n<|grad(rho)|> [rho/m] [rho 2/m 4] ) [rho 2/m 2]\n<1/R 2> [/m 2]\nenclosed volume [-]\ndV/drho [m**3/rho] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_fluxav_g.html"},{"title":"AJAX_I – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_I(nrho_r, rho_r, iflag, message, CUR_I_R, CUR_F_R, CUR_IMN_R, CUR_IMX_R, CUR_FMN_R, CUR_FMX_R) AJAX_I gets the enclosed toroidal and external poloidal currents for a set of\n  flux surfaces from the covariant components of B, as well as maximum and\n  minimum values for use as a diagnostic on the accuracy of the stream function References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Declaration of input variables\nAllocate covariant B field array Perform integrals of covariant B components on each surface Over radial nodes Over toroidal nodes Over poloidal nodes Get cylindrical coordinates and metrics\nCheck messages\nGet covariant B components\nCheck messages\nOver poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Toroidal current\nOver toroidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Poloidal current\nOver poloidal nodes Over toroidal nodes Over radial nodes Check whether axial values are requested\nUse value of second node Cleanup and exit Deallocate arrays Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nrho_r no. of radial nodes [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rho_r (:) radial nodes [rho] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional output variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: CUR_I_R (:) enclosed toroidal current [A]\nexternal poloidal current [A]\nminimum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nmaximum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nminimum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A]\nmaximum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: CUR_F_R (:) enclosed toroidal current [A]\nexternal poloidal current [A]\nminimum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nmaximum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nminimum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A]\nmaximum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: CUR_IMN_R (:) enclosed toroidal current [A]\nexternal poloidal current [A]\nminimum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nmaximum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nminimum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A]\nmaximum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: CUR_IMX_R (:) enclosed toroidal current [A]\nexternal poloidal current [A]\nminimum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nmaximum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nminimum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A]\nmaximum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: CUR_FMN_R (:) enclosed toroidal current [A]\nexternal poloidal current [A]\nminimum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nmaximum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nminimum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A]\nmaximum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: CUR_FMX_R (:) enclosed toroidal current [A]\nexternal poloidal current [A]\nminimum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nmaximum toroidal current on AJAX toroidal grid [A]\nminimum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A]\nmaximum poloidal current on AJAX poloidal grid [A] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_i.html"},{"title":"AJAX_MAGFLUX – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_MAGFLUX(nrho_r, rho_r, iflag, message, IOTABAR_R, Q_R, PHIPRM_R, PSIPRM_R, PHI_R, PSI_R) AJAX_MAGFLUX gets poloidal and toroidal magnetic fluxes References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004\n  W.A.Houlberg, named DO loop on EXIT 1/2005 Declaration of input variables\nInternal values\nCheck whether values outside R,Z domain are requested (nr is last point inside)\nOver nodes Over nodes Get temporary base quantities for phiprm and iotabar Inside MHD solution domain\nOver radial nodes Over radial nodes Extrapolate outside with constant slope in iotabar Return the appropriate quantity Rotational transform\nSafety factor\nd(Phi)/d(rho)\nd(Psi)/d(rho)\nTotal toroidal flux\nTotal poloidal flux\nCheck messages\nOver radial nodes Over radial nodes Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nrho_r no. of radial nodes [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rho_r (:) radial nodes [rho] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of output variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: IOTABAR_R (:) rotational transform = d(Psi)/d(Phi) [-]\nsafety factor = d(Phi)/d(Psi) [-]\nd(Phi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\nd(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntoroidal flux [Wb]\npoloidal flux [Wb] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: Q_R (:) rotational transform = d(Psi)/d(Phi) [-]\nsafety factor = d(Phi)/d(Psi) [-]\nd(Phi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\nd(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntoroidal flux [Wb]\npoloidal flux [Wb] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: PHIPRM_R (:) rotational transform = d(Psi)/d(Phi) [-]\nsafety factor = d(Phi)/d(Psi) [-]\nd(Phi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\nd(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntoroidal flux [Wb]\npoloidal flux [Wb] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: PSIPRM_R (:) rotational transform = d(Psi)/d(Phi) [-]\nsafety factor = d(Phi)/d(Psi) [-]\nd(Phi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\nd(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntoroidal flux [Wb]\npoloidal flux [Wb] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: PHI_R (:) rotational transform = d(Psi)/d(Phi) [-]\nsafety factor = d(Phi)/d(Psi) [-]\nd(Phi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\nd(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntoroidal flux [Wb]\npoloidal flux [Wb] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: PSI_R (:) rotational transform = d(Psi)/d(Phi) [-]\nsafety factor = d(Phi)/d(Psi) [-]\nd(Phi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\nd(Psi)/d(rho) [Wb/rho]\ntoroidal flux [Wb]\npoloidal flux [Wb] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_magflux.html"},{"title":"AJAX_SHAPE – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_SHAPE(nrho_r, rho_r, iflag, message, ZETA, SHIFT_R, ELONG_R, TRIANG_R, RMAX_R, RMIN_R, ZMAX_R, ZMIN_R, RBOT_R, RTOP_R) AJAX_SHAPE gets shift, elongation, and triangularity References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004\n  W.A.Houlberg, named DO loop on EXIT 1/2005 Declaration of input variables\nNull local values\nSet the toroidal angle for the calculations\nCheck whether values outside R,Z domain are requested (nr is last point inside)\nOver nodes Over nodes Half diameter and center of plasma boundary Find coordinates where dR/dtheta=0 on inside for R_min\nCheck messages\nFind coordinates where dR/dtheta=0 on outside for R_max\nCheck messages\nMajor radius of center of plasma boundary\nMinor radius = half diameter Find inside, outside (dR/theta=0) and top, bottom (dZ/dtheta=0) of each surface Over radial nodes dR/dtheta=0 on inside\nCheck messages\ndR/dtheta=0 on outside\nCheck messages\ndZ/dtheta=0 on bottom\nCheck messages\ndZ/dtheta=0 on top\nCheck messages\nOver radial nodes Shift Initialization\nShift relative to center of outer surface Set axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to external grid points outside R,Z domain Elongation Initialization\nElongation is total height over total width\nSet axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to external grid points outside R,Z domain Triangularity Initialization\nTriangularity - average of upper and lower\nSet axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages\nExtrapolate to external grid points outside R,Z domain Maximum R Initialization\nTo cover odd-shaped plasmas, look for maxima near pi/4 and 7pi/4\nOver radial nodes Check messages\nCheck messages\nOver radial nodes Set axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages Minimum R Initialization\nTo cover odd-shaped plasmas, look for minima near 3pi/4 and 5pi/4\nOver radial nodes Check messages\nCheck messages\nOver radial nodes Set axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages Maximum Z Initialization\nSet axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages Minimum Z Initialization\nSet axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages R at maximum Z Initialization\nSet axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages R at minimum Z Initialization\nSet axial value\nInterpolate to external grid points inside R,Z domain\nCheck messages Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nrho_r no. of radial nodes [-] real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rho_r (:) radial nodes [rho] Declaration of output variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional input variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(in), optional :: ZETA toroidal plane for the shape [-]\n                        !!=0 by default Declaration of optional output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: SHIFT_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: ELONG_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: TRIANG_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: RMAX_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: RMIN_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: ZMAX_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: ZMIN_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: RBOT_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: RTOP_R (:) shift [-]\nelongation [-]\ntriangularity [-]\nmaximum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum R of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nmaximum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nminimum Z of plasma in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMIN_R in zeta plane [m]\nR at ZMAX_R in zeta plane [m] Declaration of local variables","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_shape.html"},{"title":"AJAX_GLOBALS – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_GLOBALS(iflag, message, R000, PHITOT, RHOMAX, RHOMIN, SIGNBP, SIGNBT, NPER, NRHO, NTHETA, NZETA) AJAX_GLOBALS gets global characteristics of the data References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004 Declaration of output variables Return values Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error Declaration of optional output variables character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character] real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: R000 coefficient of (m,n)=(0,0) mode for R at axis [m]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb]\ninner radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nouter radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nsign of the poloidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is down on outside\nsign of the toroidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is counterclockwise from top view Initialization Null output real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: PHITOT coefficient of (m,n)=(0,0) mode for R at axis [m]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb]\ninner radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nouter radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nsign of the poloidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is down on outside\nsign of the toroidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is counterclockwise from top view Initialization Null output real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: RHOMAX coefficient of (m,n)=(0,0) mode for R at axis [m]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb]\ninner radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nouter radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nsign of the poloidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is down on outside\nsign of the toroidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is counterclockwise from top view Initialization Null output real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: RHOMIN coefficient of (m,n)=(0,0) mode for R at axis [m]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb]\ninner radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nouter radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nsign of the poloidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is down on outside\nsign of the toroidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is counterclockwise from top view Initialization Null output real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: SIGNBP coefficient of (m,n)=(0,0) mode for R at axis [m]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb]\ninner radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nouter radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nsign of the poloidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is down on outside\nsign of the toroidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is counterclockwise from top view Initialization Null output real(kind=rspec), intent(out), optional :: SIGNBT coefficient of (m,n)=(0,0) mode for R at axis [m]\ntotal toroidal flux [Wb]\ninner radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nouter radial boundary of R,Z domain [rho]\nsign of the poloidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is down on outside\nsign of the toroidal magnetic field [-]\npositive is counterclockwise from top view Initialization Null output integer, intent(out), optional :: NPER number of field periods, =0 for axisymmetry [-]\nnumber of radial nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of poloidal nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of toroidal nodes in internal data [-] integer, intent(out), optional :: NRHO number of field periods, =0 for axisymmetry [-]\nnumber of radial nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of poloidal nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of toroidal nodes in internal data [-] integer, intent(out), optional :: NTHETA number of field periods, =0 for axisymmetry [-]\nnumber of radial nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of poloidal nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of toroidal nodes in internal data [-] integer, intent(out), optional :: NZETA number of field periods, =0 for axisymmetry [-]\nnumber of radial nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of poloidal nodes in internal data [-]\nnumber of toroidal nodes in internal data [-]","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_globals.html"},{"title":"AJAX_MINMAX_RZ – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine AJAX_MINMAX_RZ(l_rminmax, r_flx, r_cyl, iflag, message) AJAX_MINMAX_RZ gets maximum or minimum of R or Z References:\n  W.A.Houlberg, F90 free format 8/2004\n  W.A.Houlberg, named DO loop on EXIT 1/2005 Declaration of input variables\nNull local values\nIndex for derivative\nd(R)/d(theta)\nd(Z)/d(theta) Find extrema Check messages\nCheck messages\nNormally 1 or 2 iterations are required\nOver iteration Check messages\nOver iteration Cleanup and exit Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical, intent(in) :: l_rminmax switch to select search for R or Z [logical]\n=.TRUE. find maximum or minimum R\n=.FALSE. find maximum or minimum Z Declaration of input/output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(inout) :: r_flx (:) flux coordinates (rho,theta,zeta) [rho,rad,rad] Declaration of output variables real(kind=rspec), intent(out) :: r_cyl (:) cylindrical coordinates (R,phi,Z) [m,rad,m] Declaration of local variables integer, intent(out) :: iflag error and warning flag [-]\n=-1 warning\n=0 none\n=1 error character(len=*), intent(out) :: message warning or error message [character]","tags":"","url":"proc/ajax_minmax_rz.html"},{"title":"PRL – PELLETS","text":"public  subroutine PRL(irunid, idiag, Bt, Rm, am, chi0, rpel, rhop, pnum, vpel, n_r, te_r, ne_r, q_r, tea_r, nea_r, rho_r, nump) **\nneinf_pr = 1.0e14\nteinf_pr = 5000.0  !5 kev q0, qa, and qfact have not been given values, obsolete coding\nq(i)=q0+qa (rtw(i) xloc) qfact  !q profile is known\nq(i)=260.0/(Rmtw(i) Rin)  !Keep Rq constant **   &\nCOS((lc_pr/(q_prl(ixloc) rm_pr)) xcenn_pr(i)) COS((lc_pr xintn_pr(i)/(q_prl(ixloc) rm_pr)) xcenn_pr(i)) Eqn 25 of PoP 2000\n Note this is psi_twiddle - see PoP2000 Eqn 25. **\nteinf_pr = 5000.0\nneinf_pr = 1.0e14 **          qhatt=qhat_pr Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: irunid integer, intent(in) :: idiag real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: Bt real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: Rm real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: am real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: chi0 real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rpel real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: rhop real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: pnum real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: vpel integer, intent(in) :: n_r real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: te_r (:) real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: ne_r (:) real(kind=rspec), intent(in) :: q_r (:) real(kind=rspec), intent(out) :: tea_r (:) real(kind=rspec), i